# Append-only state directories.
#
# `merge=union` keeps BOTH sides' lines when two branches add to the same file,
# which is exactly right for a file that is only ever added to. It is WRONG for
# any file where a side rewrites an existing line — union would silently keep
# both versions. Do not widen these patterns to the lane status files.
docs/progress/log/**   merge=union

# NOTE: a `docs/memory/**` rule was removed 2026-08-30 — no such directory exists or is
# planned. The decision log is the single file `docs/MEMORY.md`, which is coordinator-written
# and must NOT get merge=union: it is rewritten in place (statuses flip, questions close), and
# union would silently keep both versions of an edited line.
